---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.avif";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";

// STARTER_CONTENT: replace the hero artwork and its alt text below, then
// remove this comment.
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="A lecture theatre reduced to flat gold and black shapes, rows of seats sweeping past the frame, in a two-ink risograph print"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Alongside a semester-long calibration diary — ranges committed before you
    know the answer — each week gives you a different way estimates go
    wrong: decomposition, borrowed evidence, disagreement, pressure,
    aggregation, stakes, forecasting. You decompose real quantities into
    chains of assumptions, give each one a stated range, and defend it when
    someone leans on it. The two pieces of graded work are the diary itself
    and one real, contested estimate, cross-examined in front of the class.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who has to give a number to someone who will act on it, without
    time to run a full study first — the course teaches judgment under
    incomplete evidence, not formulas.
  </p>

  <h2>How the course runs</h2>
  <p>
    Each teaching week runs one lecture, delivered by the course convenor,
    and one tutorial per student, chosen from four weekly timeslots — all
    four cover the same session content, taught by one of three tutors.
    There is a one-week teaching break between Weeks 5 and 6, with no
    lecture or tutorial that week. Full times, tutors and the semester
    overview are on the {sessionLabels.plural} page.
  </p>

  <h2>Assessment</h2>
  <p>Two pieces of work, no final examination:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Calibration Diary</strong> — 45%</li>
    <li><strong>Client Estimate &amp; Estimate Court</strong> — 55%</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title="Lectures" href="/lectures/">
      <p>What each week's lecture covers, and when.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The weekly tutorial timetable and what happens in each session.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
